# Local art working directory. Source PNGs + webp exports for canonical art.
# The shipped assets live in Supabase storage (downtime-images/srd/), so these
# are working files, not build inputs — keeping 17MB of raw PNGs out of a public
# repo. Back them up outside git if you want the originals.
art-src/
.vercel
.env*
# Vite's isolated localdb env contains only the Supabase CLI's public defaults.
!config/env/localdb/.env

# Bun lockfile. This project is npm: CI runs `npm ci` with `cache: npm`
# (.github/workflows/test.yml), package-lock.json is the authoritative tree, and
# package.json's `allowScripts` field — six deliberate install-script verdicts,
# reasoned out in docs/npm-install-scripts.md — is an npm feature that bun does
# not read (it uses `trustedDependencies` instead). A tracked bun.lock therefore
# adds a second, unvalidated dependency tree that CI never checks, and it was
# removed for that reason. Ignored rather than merely deleted so a local
# `bun install` cannot quietly commit it back.
bun.lock
bun.lockb

# graphify knowledge-graph output. Not committed, for two reasons beyond size:
# every node carries a `source_location` and the manifest a `scan_root`, so the
# files are full of absolute local paths (/Users/<name>/...) — and this repo is
# public. The graph is also a derived artifact: `/graphify .` rebuilds it, and a
# committed copy would silently rot against the code it describes. Includes the
# extraction cache and cost.json (token spend), which are per-machine anyway.
graphify-out/
